Package: nocs-appliance
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Jorge Valencia <jorjazo@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: nocs, network-manager, dnsmasq-base, iw, nftables, chrony, gpsd, avahi-daemon
Section: science
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/jorjazo/nocs
Description: make this computer a dedicated NOCS box
 NOCS runs at the telescope and is operated from a phone, tablet or desktop
 browser, on top of INDI drivers.
 .
 This package turns a computer into the NOCS appliance, as on the Raspberry Pi
 image: NetworkManager runs the network (access point, home Wi-Fi and the
 fallback), a firewall closes indiserver and PHD2 to the network, nocsd serves
 port 80, the privileged helper may do everything nocsd asks, updates are only
 downloaded, and a USB GPS sets the clock. Do not install it on a computer that
 is used for anything else.
